        },
        "pain_h": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "If this sounds like your walks",
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "pain_t": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<ul><li>Your dog pulls like a freight train the second the front door opens.</li><li>Your shoulder or lower back hurts after every walk.</li><li>You've tried a back-clip harness, a slip lead, maybe a head halter. Nothing stuck.</li><li>Bikes and runners on the shared path make you tense up before they even get close.</li></ul><p>That isn't a bad dog. It's gear that gives them something to lean into.</p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "pain_cap",
        "pain_h",
        "pain_t"
      ],
      "settings": {
