    "faq": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_1": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Will it stop my dog pulling?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Most dogs pull noticeably less on the first walk because pulling stops getting them anywhere. Some determined dogs take a few walks. That's why you get 60 days, not 60 minutes.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_2": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is the difference between the front and back clips?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>The front (chest) clip redirects a pull sideways, back towards you. Use it on busy paths and for training. The back clip lets your dog walk freely once the lead stays slack. Switch back to the front clip the moment pulling returns.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_3": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What if my dog is between sizes?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Go up. Thick double coat? Go up. Wrong size costs you nothing: free swap within 60 days.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "faq_4": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long does delivery take?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>We ship within one business day. Australia Post standard (free): 2–4 business days metro, 3–6 regional, longer for remote WA and NT. Express (A$9.95): 1–3 business days.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
